   "id": "29196c62",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# A-001 Agent — Skills + Progressive Disclosure + Memory\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the **second workshop notebook**.\n",
    "\n",
    "It adds only three concepts on top of SQL + RAG:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Skills** — Markdown instructions describing how the agent should perform a task.\n",
    "2. **Progressive Disclosure** — read the small skill catalog first, then load only the selected skill file.\n",
    "3. **Memory** — keep a small amount of conversational context such as the current asset and previous skill.\n",
    "\n",
    "### RAG settings\n",
    "\n",
    "- PDF only\n",
    "- Chunk size: **400**\n",
    "- Chunk overlap: **100**\n",
    "- Retrieval: **Top K = 3**\n",
    "- Embedding: **Databricks Qwen3 Embedding 0.6B**\n",
    "- Embedding dimensions: **1024**\n",
    "- Chat model: **Databricks Llama 3.3 70B Instruct**\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "User Question\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "skills_catalog.md\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "Choose Skill\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "Load only selected skill.md\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "Memory Context\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "SQL / RAG / Both\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "LLM\n",
    "      ↓\n",
    "Human-review answer\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "**Memory is context, not evidence.** SQL and the PDF documents remain the evidence sources."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb142bac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Install libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "LlamaIndex handles PDF loading, chunking, indexing and retrieval.\n",
    "\n",
    "We do **not** download a Hugging Face embedding model. Embeddings come from the Databricks-hosted Qwen3 embedding endpoint."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "883c6e70",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%pip install -q llama-index-core llama-index-readers-file pypdf mlflow"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5358e8a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Configure Databricks and the embedding model\n",
    "\n",
    "These are your actual workspace locations.\n",
    "\n",
    "The small adapter below lets LlamaIndex call the Databricks embedding endpoint through `mlflow.deployments`.\n",
    "\n",
    "This keeps the example inside Databricks and removes the Hugging Face dependency."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "734bd262",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from typing import List\n",
    "\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\\n",\n    "from llama_index.core import SimpleDirectoryReader, VectorStoreIndex, Settings\n",
    "from llama_index.core.embeddings import BaseEmbedding\n",
    "from mlflow.deployments import get_deploy_client\n",
    "\n",
    "DOCUMENT_FOLDER = \"/Workspace/Nuclear_Enterprise_360/A001 Documents\"\n",
    "SKILLS_FOLDER = \"/Workspace/Nuclear_Enterprise_360/02_Agent_Skills\"\n",
    "ASSET_TABLE = \"workspace.nuclear_enterprise_360.asset_360\"\n",
    "\n",
    "EMBEDDING_MODEL = \"databricks-qwen3-embedding-0-6b\"\n",
    "CHAT_MODEL = \"databricks-meta-llama-3-3-70b-instruct\"\n",
    "EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS = 1024\n",
    "\n",
    "Settings.chunk_size = 400\n",
    "Settings.chunk_overlap = 100\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "class DatabricksQwenEmbedding(BaseEmbedding):\n",
    "    model_name: str = EMBEDDING_MODEL\n",
    "    dimensions: int = EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _embed(self, text: str) -> List[float]:\n",
    "        client = get_deploy_client(\"databricks\")\n",
    "        response = client.predict(\n",
    "            endpoint=self.model_name,\n",
    "            inputs={\n",
    "                \"input\": text,\n",
    "                \"dimensions\": self.dimensions\n",
    "            }\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        return response[\"data\"][0][\"embedding\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _get_query_embedding(self, query: str) -> List[float]:\n",
    "        return self._embed(query)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def _get_text_embedding(self, text: str) -> List[float]:\n",
    "        return self._embed(text)\n",
    "\n",
    "    async def _aget_query_embedding(self, query: str) -> List[float]:\n",
    "        return self._embed(query)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Settings.embed_model = DatabricksQwenEmbedding()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Documents :\", DOCUMENT_FOLDER)\n",
    "print(\"Skills    :\", SKILLS_FOLDER)\n",
    "print(\"SQL table :\", ASSET_TABLE)\n",
    "print(\"Embedding :\", EMBEDDING_MODEL)\n",
    "print(\"Dimensions:\", EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a0f9fe87",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Validate PDFs and the Databricks embedding endpoint\n",
    "\n",
    "Before building RAG, check two things:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. the PDFs are visible;\n",
    "2. the embedding endpoint returns a 1024-dimensional vector."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d73de636",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pdf_files = sorted(Path(DOCUMENT_FOLDER).glob(\"*.pdf\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"PDF files found:\", len(pdf_files))\n",
    "for pdf in pdf_files:\n",
    "    print(\"-\", pdf.name)\n",
    "\n",
    "vector = Settings.embed_model.get_text_embedding(\n",
    "    \"A-001 cooling water pump reliability review\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(\"Embedding dimensions:\", len(vector))\n",
    "print(\"Embedding test: OK\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c73c9458",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Build the simple LlamaIndex RAG retriever\n",
    "\n",
    "LlamaIndex now performs the repetitive work:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "PDFs\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "SimpleDirectoryReader\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Chunking 400 / overlap 100\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Databricks Qwen embeddings\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "VectorStoreIndex\n",
    "  ↓\n",
    "Top K = 3\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "No manual page extraction, custom chunking function, or cosine-similarity code is needed."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "dd50f4ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "documents = SimpleDirectoryReader(\n",
    "    input_dir=DOCUMENT_FOLDER,\n",
    "    required_exts=[\".pdf\"]\n",
    ").load_data()\n",
    "\n",
    "index = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)\n",
    "retriever = index.as_retriever(similarity_top_k=3)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Loaded document objects:\", len(documents))\n",
    "print(\"Chunk size: 400 | Overlap: 100 | Top K: 3\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4c28c7d7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Define the three tools\n",
    "\n",
    "A **tool** is something the agent can call.\n",
    "\n",
    "- `sql_tool()` → structured A-001 facts\n",
    "- `rag_tool(question)` → top 3 PDF chunks\n",
    "- `llm(prompt)` → final Databricks LLM response"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "165ecb9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def sql_tool():\n",
    "    row = spark.sql(f\"\"\"\n",
    "        SELECT\n",
    "            asset_id,\n",
    "            asset_name,\n",
    "            criticality,\n",
    "            health_score,\n",
    "            risk_level,\n",
    "            open_work_orders,\n",
    "            high_priority_open_work,\n",
    "            follow_up_findings\n",
    "        FROM {ASSET_TABLE}\n",
    "        WHERE asset_id = 'A-001'\n",
    "        LIMIT 1\n",
    "    \"\"\").first()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return row.asDict() if row else {}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def rag_tool(question):\n",
    "    results = retriever.retrieve(question)\n",
    "\n",
    "    return \"\\n\\n\".join(\n",
    "        f\"SOURCE: {r.node.metadata.get('file_name', 'PDF')}\\n{r.node.get_content()}\"\n",
    "        for r in results\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def llm(prompt):\n",
    "    client = get_deploy_client(\"databricks\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    response = client.predict(\n",
    "        endpoint=CHAT_MODEL,\n",
    "        inputs={\n",
    "            \"messages\": [\n",
    "                {\n",
    "                    \"role\": \"system\",\n",
    "                    \"content\": (\n",
    "                        \"Use only the supplied evidence. \"\n",
    "                        \"Do not diagnose equipment failure. \"\n",
    "                        \"Do not authorize maintenance. \"\n",
    "                        \"Final operational decisions remain with a qualified human.\"\n",
    "                    )\n",
    "                },\n",
    "                {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}\n",
    "            ],\n",
    "            \"temperature\": 0.1,\n",
    "            \"max_tokens\": 700\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    return response[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a3b56ab1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Skills and `skills_catalog.md`\n",
    "\n",
    "A **skill** is a Markdown instruction file that tells the agent how to perform a business capability.\n",
    "\n",
    "Your folder is:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "/Workspace/Nuclear_Enterprise_360/02_Agent_Skills/\n",
    "\n",
    "skills_catalog.md\n",
    "asset_summary.md\n",
    "approved_procedure.md\n",
    "reliability_review.md\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Three skills\n",
    "\n",
    "**asset_summary**\n",
    "- SQL only\n",
    "- return current structured facts\n",
    "\n",
    "**approved_procedure**\n",
    "- RAG only\n",
    "- identify current approved procedure\n",
    "- reject DRAFT and SUPERSEDED as current authority\n",
    "\n",
    "**reliability_review**\n",
    "- SQL + RAG\n",
    "- produce an evidence-backed review briefing\n",
    "- final decision remains with a human\n",
    "\n",
    "### What is `skills_catalog.md`?\n",
    "\n",
    "It is the small menu the agent sees first.\n",
    "\n",
    "The detailed instructions for all skills are not loaded into the prompt yet."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b3ead012",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SKILLS_CATALOG = f\"{SKILLS_FOLDER}/skills_catalog.md\"\n",
    "\n",
    "SKILL_FILES = {\n",
    "    \"asset_summary\": f\"{SKILLS_FOLDER}/asset_summary.md\",\n",
    "    \"approved_procedure\": f\"{SKILLS_FOLDER}/approved_procedure.md\",\n",
    "    \"reliability_review\": f\"{SKILLS_FOLDER}/reliability_review.md\"\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def read_md(path):\n",
    "    return Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# LEVEL 1: read only the small catalog\n",
    "catalog = read_md(SKILLS_CATALOG)\n",
    "print(catalog)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7df59c99",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Progressive Disclosure\n",
    "\n",
    "Progressive disclosure means:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Question\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Read small catalog\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Choose one skill\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Load only that skill.md\n",
    "   ↓\n",
    "Use only the tools required\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "\"What is the health score?\"\n",
    "→ asset_summary.md\n",
    "→ SQL\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Which procedure is approved?\"\n",
    "→ approved_procedure.md\n",
    "→ RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Should A-001 be escalated?\"\n",
    "→ reliability_review.md\n",
    "→ SQL + RAG\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The key point: **do not load all detailed skills for every question.**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "13d5a9f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def choose_skill(question):\n",
    "    q = question.lower()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if any(word in q for word in [\n",
    "        \"review\", \"investigate\", \"escalate\", \"assessment\", \"should\"\n",
    "    ]):\n",
    "        return \"reliability_review\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    if any(word in q for word in [\n",
    "        \"procedure\", \"approved\", \"guidance\", \"version\"\n",
    "    ]):\n",
    "        return \"approved_procedure\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    return \"asset_summary\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_selected_skill(skill_name):\n",
    "    # LEVEL 2: load only the selected detailed skill file\n",
    "    return read_md(SKILL_FILES[skill_name])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "72cb27ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Small working memory\n",
    "\n",
    "Memory gives continuity across turns.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a beginner example we keep only:\n",
    "\n",
    "- current asset;\n",
    "- previous skill;\n",
    "- last two interactions.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Turn 1: \"Investigate A-001\"\n",
    "Memory: current asset = A-001\n",
    "\n",
    "Turn 2: \"Which procedure applies to it?\"\n",
    "Memory helps interpret \"it\" as A-001\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Memory does not replace SQL or RAG evidence."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5037f929",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "memory = {\n",
    "    \"asset_id\": \"A-001\",\n",
    "    \"last_skill\": None,\n",
    "    \"history\": []\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def memory_context():\n",
    "    recent = memory[\"history\"][-2:]\n",
    "    recent_text = \"\\n\".join(recent) if recent else \"No previous turns\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    return f\"\"\"\n",
    "Current asset: {memory['asset_id']}\n",
    "Previous skill: {memory['last_skill']}\n",
    "Recent turns:\n",
    "{recent_text}\n",
    "\"\"\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cd9e150d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. One simple agent\n",
    "\n",
    "This function connects everything:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. choose the skill;\n",
    "2. load only that skill `.md`;\n",
    "3. read memory;\n",
    "4. call SQL, RAG, or both;\n",
    "5. ask the LLM for the answer;\n",
    "6. update memory.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the whole beginner implementation of **Skills + Progressive Disclosure + Memory**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cccac8d1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def agent(question):\n",
    "    # 1. Select skill\n",
    "    skill = choose_skill(question)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 2. Progressive disclosure: load ONLY selected skill\n",
    "    skill_instructions = load_selected_skill(skill)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 3. Use only the tools required by this skill\n",
    "    sql_evidence = (\n",
    "        sql_tool()\n",
    "        if skill in [\"asset_summary\", \"reliability_review\"]\n",
    "        else \"Not needed for this skill\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    rag_evidence = (\n",
    "        rag_tool(question)\n",
    "        if skill in [\"approved_procedure\", \"reliability_review\"]\n",
    "        else \"Not needed for this skill\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 4. Final prompt\n",
    "    prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
    "SELECTED SKILL:\n",
    "{skill}\n",
    "\n",
    "SKILL INSTRUCTIONS:\n",
    "{skill_instructions}\n",
    "\n",
    "MEMORY:\n",
    "{memory_context()}\n",
    "\n",
    "CURRENT QUESTION:\n",
    "{question}\n",
    "\n",
    "SQL EVIDENCE:\n",
    "{sql_evidence}\n",
    "\n",
    "TOP 3 RAG EVIDENCE:\n",
    "{rag_evidence}\n",
    "\n",
    "IMPORTANT:\n",
    "- APPROVED documents are current authority.\n",
    "- DRAFT documents are not current authority.\n",
    "- SUPERSEDED documents are historical only.\n",
    "- Memory is context, not evidence.\n",
    "- Do not diagnose equipment failure.\n",
    "- Do not authorize maintenance.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    answer = llm(prompt)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 5. Update memory\n",
    "    memory[\"last_skill\"] = skill\n",
    "    memory[\"history\"].append(\n",
    "        f\"Question: {question} | Skill: {skill}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Selected skill:\", skill)\n",
    "    print(\"Loaded skill file:\", SKILL_FILES[skill])\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "782c1d3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Run the three workshop examples\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question 1** → SQL skill\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question 2** → RAG skill and only `approved_procedure.md`\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question 3** → SQL + RAG and only `reliability_review.md`\n",
    "\n",
    "Memory remains available across the three turns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1551abce",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"QUESTION 1\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(agent(\"What is the current health condition of A-001?\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\\nQUESTION 2\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(agent(\"Which inspection procedure is currently approved for it?\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\\nQUESTION 3\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(agent(\"Should it be escalated for qualified reliability review?\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\n\\nFINAL MEMORY\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 80)\n",
    "print(memory)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fcb0dc14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Final Mental Model\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "TOOLS\n",
    "= what the agent can call\n",
    "\n",
    "SKILLS\n",
    "= how the agent should perform a capability\n",
    "\n",
    "PROGRESSIVE DISCLOSURE\n",
    "= load only the selected skill instructions\n",
    "\n",
    "MEMORY\n",
    "= small conversational context retained across turns\n",
    "\n",
    "EVIDENCE\n",
    "= SQL + current PDF evidence\n",
    "\n",
    "HUMAN REVIEW\n",
    "= final authority for high-impact action\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "For A-001:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Health question\n",
    "→ asset_summary\n",
    "→ SQL\n",
    "\n",
    "Procedure question\n",
    "→ approved_procedure\n",
    "→ RAG\n",
    "\n",
    "Reliability review question\n",
    "→ reliability_review\n",
    "→ SQL + RAG\n",
    "→ Human review\n",
    "```"
   ]
  }
